Shelldeck — how to run (Ubuntu)

1. Make it executable and start it:
      chmod +x Shelldeck-x86_64.AppImage
      ./Shelldeck-x86_64.AppImage
   (or right-click → Properties → Permissions → "Allow executing", then double-click)

2. It opens your browser at http://127.0.0.1:<port>. On first launch it asks you
   to create YOUR OWN master password. Everything you save (servers, keys, VPN)
   is encrypted with it and stays on your machine, in ~/.shelldeck.

3. For the one-click VPN feature only, install OpenVPN once:
      sudo apt install openvpn
   (SSH, SFTP and everything else work without it.)

4. Press F1 inside the app for the full manual. Highlights:
      - Import  -> pull your servers in from ~/.ssh/config or Asbru
      - Shared file -> import a colleague's exported setup
      - Export  -> share YOUR setup (no passwords/keys ever leave)
      - Ctrl-click a connection to open it beside another; then
        "broadcast" types one command into every terminal at once
      - The whole list is keyboard-navigable (Tab, Enter to open)
      - sun/moon at the top right switches light/dark

If it won't start with "libfuse.so.2: cannot open", either:
      sudo apt install libfuse2
   or run it without FUSE:
      ./Shelldeck-x86_64.AppImage --appimage-extract-and-run

Verify the download is intact (optional):
      sha256sum Shelldeck-x86_64.AppImage
   should print:
      __SHA256__

Nothing is shared between users and nothing is sent anywhere — each person's
vault is private to their own machine. Press F1 in the app for the full guide.
